   $q$Which statement best expresses a central theme of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Helping someone well means understanding what they truly need, not just what seems wrong.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Older people are not able to learn how to use new technology.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Medicine reminders should have large buttons and very loud chimes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-theme"},{"text":"Learning to code is the best way to solve problems within a family.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Helping someone well means understanding what they truly need, not just what seems wrong.$q$, $q$Daniel solves the pill problem, but Lola's real need is connection, and he helps only once he sees that. His mother says Lola "isn't confused," so the claim about older people and technology is unsupported.$q$, 'draft', '3cde1c9f-2260-5e69-a747-46caedf46519')
