   $q$How does Rosa's argument contribute to the development of the theme?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It proves that the error was too small to affect the county's map in any way.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"accepts-character-claim"},{"text":"It shows that Rosa wants Keoni to take all the blame for the mistake.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It explains why the group earned an A on its report before the error was found.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"It offers a tempting reason to stay silent, which makes Keoni's choice to report the error more meaningful.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It offers a tempting reason to stay silent, which makes Keoni's choice to report the error more meaningful.$q$, $q$Rosa's view that "a county map would not change" gives Keoni an easy excuse he rejects. Her claim is only her opinion, and Keoni thinks a line would be drawn "in the wrong place," so it does not prove the error was harmless.$q$, 'draft', 'c72ddb49-a2f2-590c-bd6d-77bc8f5c0dc1')
