  ('52c73634-e43f-57a5-bdd0-94db9dfeffe3', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-theme-summary'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which choice is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Farah resents her driver's slow, caring habits until a substitute's efficient week leaves the bus cold and quiet, and when he returns she helps a rider herself.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Farah complains to the bus company about the delays, and Mr. Ibarra is moved to a different route.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-false-detail"},{"text":"Farah, a selfish student who only cares about homework, finally learns to be kind thanks to her wonderful bus driver.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"A substitute driver takes over Route 9 for a week in March and pulls away before an older rider can board.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Farah resents her driver's slow, caring habits until a substitute's efficient week leaves the bus cold and quiet, and when he returns she helps a rider herself.$q$, $q$The correct summary covers Farah's complaint, the substitute week, and her final action. Calling Farah "selfish" and the driver "wonderful" adds opinions that an objective summary leaves out.$q$, 'draft', 'c6ed9f45-fcff-52c9-83c0-ef74c1de5407')
