   $q$The Latin root cent means "hundred." Why is the ride called "the century"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It always starts at the break of dawn","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"It has about one hundred people riding","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It has been held for one hundred years","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-context"},{"text":"It covers a distance of one hundred miles","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It covers a distance of one hundred miles$q$, $q$Cent means "hundred," and the passage defines the century as "a one-hundred-mile ride." A century can also mean one hundred years, but the passage never says that, and it mentions "hundreds" of riders, not one hundred.$q$, 'draft', '0b0f8aee-e3a6-5cc5-afe9-bac2868278d6')
