   $q$The Latin root ped means "foot." What are the "pedals" Kwame pushes down on?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The parts of the bike that slow it down on a descent","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The parts of the bike that change the gear for a hill","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-nearby-details"},{"text":"The parts of the bike that a rider pushes with the feet","is_correct":true},{"text":"The parts of the bike that a rider grips with the hands","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The parts of the bike that a rider pushes with the feet$q$, $q$Ped means "foot," and Kwame "pushed down on the pedals in a steady rhythm" while his thighs burned. Changing gears is a separate action in the same paragraph ("shifted into his easiest gear").$q$, 'draft', '0b0f8aee-e3a6-5cc5-afe9-bac2868278d6')
