  ('586ec21e-858c-584f-aa79-8a695b15d823', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-word-parts'), null, 'easy',
   $q$The prefix uni- means "one," and the Latin root son means "sound." What does it mean that the strings "played in unison"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They played very softly so others could hear","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"They each took turns playing a single note","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"They played the same note at the same time","is_correct":true},{"text":"They played different parts that fit together","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They played the same note at the same time$q$, $q$Uni- plus son means "one sound," and the passage explains it as "every instrument on the same note at the same moment." Taking turns would not be one shared sound.$q$, 'draft', '010113db-f97d-53bd-893b-4116d3ab8a16')
