   $q$The Latin root man or manu means "hand," and script means "written." What is the conductor's "manuscript"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A set of hand signals she uses to conduct","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"A recording of the orchestra's last concert","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"A printed program handed out to the audience","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"A copy of the music she wrote out by hand","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A copy of the music she wrote out by hand$q$, $q$Manu plus script means "written by hand," and the passage says "the notes [were] inked by hand in her careful, slanted writing." Hand signals use the hand but involve no writing, so they miss the script part.$q$, 'draft', '010113db-f97d-53bd-893b-4116d3ab8a16')
