   $q$Why does the Lindqvist study fail to support the conclusion the author draws from it?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It compared handwriting with typing, not cursive with other handwriting.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It found that typed notes helped students remember more than handwritten ones.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"It measured memory after a week, which is too long to be useful.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"It studied college students, and college students never write by hand.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It compared handwriting with typing, not cursive with other handwriting.$q$, $q$The study shows that writing notes by hand helped memory, but printing by hand would count too, so it says nothing about cursive in particular. The author's leap to "cursive is essential" goes beyond what the study tested.$q$, 'draft', 'f414b75c-54a2-5952-b620-2f28e72e1228')
