-- Passage rg10-argument-evidence-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('3c3063f8-3bed-5a86-9728-c883a732d97f', 'rg10-argument-evidence-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-argument-evidence'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Smart Streetlights Will Pay for Themselves$q$, $q$Harlow Mills should replace all 2,400 of its streetlights with smart LED lights that dim to a quarter of their brightness when sensors detect no people or cars nearby. The change would save money, protect the night sky and bring our town into the present.

The savings are real. Last year the town installed smart lights along Orchard Avenue as a test. Over twelve months, those forty lights used 61 percent less electricity than the old lights they replaced, according to the town's utility bills. If the whole town saw similar results, we would save more than $150,000 a year.

The new lights would also cost the town nothing to install. The council would simply approve a $400,000 bond, and the energy savings would repay it within three years.

Smart lights would make our streets safer, too. Everyone knows that a brighter street is always a safer street, and the new lights would keep our neighborhoods better protected than ever before. Since they would spend most of the night dimmed, they would also reduce the glare that hides the stars from backyard astronomers.

Finally, nearly every modern town in the region has already adopted smart lighting. Harlow Mills should not be the last community stuck with outdated technology.

The town has tested this idea and seen the results on Orchard Avenue. Now it is time to finish the job.$q$, 'draft')
