  ('f177d0f9-6bcc-53de-a3d8-98abf3539fb5', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-authors-purpose'), null, 'medium',
   $q$What is the effect of the short sentence "We could." at the start of the second paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It announces that the museum has decided to restore the quilt in response to the visitors' requests.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It reveals that the staff is unsure whether it has the training needed to do a restoration well.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-concession"},{"text":"It concedes that the museum has the skill to restore the quilt, so its choice not to is clearly deliberate.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that the author agrees with visitors that the quilt would look better if it were repaired.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It concedes that the museum has the skill to restore the quilt, so its choice not to is clearly deliberate.$q$, $q$By admitting the museum could restore the quilt, the author shows that leaving it alone is a principled decision, which strengthens his credibility. The "But" that follows makes clear the museum will not restore it.$q$, 'draft', '6c81c09c-9abe-5798-b04e-1be1002118ed')
