   $q$What is the effect of the sentences "That is not a grand plan. It will not win design awards." in the final paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They admit the plan is likely to fail, which shows the author expects the city to reject her request.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-concession"},{"text":"They suggest that the author would prefer a more expensive plan that could win attention for the city.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-viewpoint"},{"text":"They criticize the city's designers for caring more about awards than about the needs of residents.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They downplay the plan's ambition so it seems easy to approve, while the last sentence gives it a larger meaning.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They downplay the plan's ambition so it seems easy to approve, while the last sentence gives it a larger meaning.$q$, $q$By calling her goal modest, the author makes it hard to refuse, and the final sentence then says it will show residents "this city expects them to stay a while." Nothing suggests she expects failure; she presents the plan as practical.$q$, 'draft', '2fc06731-7ede-5214-b1b1-e08f9aa49554')
