  ('ab3536f1-2569-5f74-8c50-adcecd93411c', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-authors-purpose'), null, 'medium',
   $q$How does the author build trust with his readers in the first paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He describes his high grades in language class, so readers will see him as an expert.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He quotes a language teacher at his school, so readers will trust an adult's opinion.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He says he understood his friends' choice and nearly made it himself, so he sounds like a peer.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He criticizes his friends for quitting, so readers will want to avoid the same blame.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He says he understood his friends' choice and nearly made it himself, so he sounds like a peer.$q$, $q$"I understood. I almost did the same thing." shows sympathy with classmates who quit, which makes his advice feel like it comes from one of them. He does not mention grades, criticize friends, or quote anyone.$q$, 'draft', 'f863236c-afb5-59f4-b253-59d685a12316')
