   $q$In the first stanza, what do the lines "I tell myself I do not want her chair. / I tell myself a lot of things." suggest about the speaker?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The speaker does want the first chair but tries not to admit it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The speaker is planning to ask the conductor to switch the two chairs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The speaker has no interest in Imani's seat and is happy in second chair.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The speaker dislikes Imani and refuses to watch her play at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The speaker does want the first chair but tries not to admit it.$q$, $q$"I tell myself a lot of things" hints that the first claim is something the speaker repeats rather than believes. The speaker watches Imani closely enough to "copy" her bow arm, so the last choice contradicts the stanza.$q$, 'draft', '9519b9c5-6bf6-5851-a29a-86e757ab16fe')
