   $q$How does Mr. Castellanos's advice affect the plot?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It reveals that the judges already know Teo, so the credit line is unnecessary.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It solves Priya's problem by telling her exactly how to list a younger helper.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It raises the stakes, so crediting Teo becomes a real risk instead of an easy choice.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It convinces Priya to remove Teo's name, which causes her to lose the showcase.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It raises the stakes, so crediting Teo becomes a real risk instead of an easy choice.$q$, $q$His warning that a big credit line might hurt her chances means her choice could cost her the internship, making it meaningful. She does the opposite of removing Teo's name, printing it in letters as tall as her own.$q$, 'draft', '94d714ad-1d2b-5673-adb0-305456ae689a')
