values
  ('285316e7-8cd2-5c6d-ba15-20cf97e4b45e', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-character-setting-plot'), null, 'medium',
   $q$"The heron found it ridiculous. Privately, the heron also counted the kingfisher's catches." What do these sentences reveal about the heron?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The heron is keeping count to report the kingfisher for taking too many fish.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Beneath its scorn, the heron is envious and unsure whether its own way is best.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The heron is studying the kingfisher so that it can learn to dive the same way.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The heron honestly finds the kingfisher funny and has no other feelings about it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Beneath its scorn, the heron is envious and unsure whether its own way is best.$q$, $q$Calling the kingfisher ridiculous while secretly counting catches that are "more than its own" shows mixed feelings: scorn and envy. The heron never tries to dive, so learning to copy it is unsupported.$q$, 'draft', '70a8f531-992f-5c7d-9e65-b26e8767e4a4')
