  ('399b3b8f-6f1c-56eb-879b-4a864c56741d', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-character-setting-plot'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The kingfisher says, "I have been fishing it alone, and it is too quiet." How does this line complicate the kingfisher's character and shape the ending?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows its kindness comes partly from loneliness, which helps explain why it waits and welcomes the heron.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows the kingfisher is afraid of the dark pool and needs the heron to protect it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It shows the kingfisher wants the heron's pond for itself and is tricking it into leaving.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It shows the kingfisher is bragging, so it later mocks the heron for arriving so late.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows its kindness comes partly from loneliness, which helps explain why it waits and welcomes the heron.$q$, $q$Admitting the pool is "too quiet" reveals the kingfisher also needs something, company, so it waits and "moved over to make room" instead of gloating. It never mocks the heron; it "did not mention the three days."$q$, 'draft', '70a8f531-992f-5c7d-9e65-b26e8767e4a4')
