   $q$How does the final sentence of Text 2 connect to the ending of the myth?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Unlike the myth, Text 2 ends with the riders thanking Dashiell by name for his careful work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Unlike the myth, Text 2 suggests that guides only matter when travelers know who made them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"Like the faded threads, the new map will soon fade and need to be redrawn by another intern.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Like the faded threads whose paths remain, the map's maker \"disappears\" while the guidance keeps helping people.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Like the faded threads whose paths remain, the map's maker "disappears" while the guidance keeps helping people.$q$, $q$The myth says the threads "have faded from sight" but the paths remain, and Text 2 says the maker "disappears" while people "find their way home." Nothing suggests the map will fade, so that choice reads the parallel too literally.$q$, 'draft', '43b4f611-d8d6-5d1f-8121-33b8d77305c2')
