  ('349705ae-e831-5838-8635-30953b715591', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-comparing-texts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$How does the point of view of Text 2 change the way the story pattern is presented?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A first-person newcomer watches the leaders make peace, adding humor and personal reflection to the pattern.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The narrator is one of the coaches, who explains why the schedule was the only fair choice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The two captains take turns narrating, so readers learn each rival's private reasons for the conflict.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"A distant narrator reports the events as a legend, just as the narrator of Text 1 does.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-point-of-view"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A first-person newcomer watches the leaders make peace, adding humor and personal reflection to the pattern.$q$, $q$Text 2 is told by a new runner ("I joined the Pell Ridge cross-country team in September") who compares the captains to "two cats." Text 1 uses a distant storytelling voice, so Text 2 does not keep that point of view.$q$, 'draft', '797ac378-440f-52e7-b9a8-fb1b3cd32b1e')
