   $q$Which theme do both texts share?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A performer who overpowers others learns that listening makes the music stronger.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Audiences care more about a soloist's skill than about the group as a whole.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"A talented performer should always play as loudly as possible to be noticed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"Musicians who practice alone become better than musicians who play in groups.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A performer who overpowers others learns that listening makes the music stronger.$q$, $q$Oriel's echo returns when she hums softly with the shepherd, and Caspian's solo sounds "bigger than before" once he listens. Both texts criticize playing over others, so the choice praising loudness reverses the theme.$q$, 'draft', 'ef91595a-cd70-58eb-906b-5331fee2fab5')
