   $q$How does the narrator of Text 2 change the way the story pattern is told?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The director tells it, explaining the teaching plan she used before the rehearsal began.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-point-of-view"},{"text":"A village storyteller tells it, using the same distant voice as the narrator of Text 1.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-texts"},{"text":"The loud performer tells it himself, so readers learn exactly why he decided to play more softly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-point-of-view"},{"text":"A quiet band member tells it, so readers see the loud performer's change through someone he used to drown out.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A quiet band member tells it, so readers see the loud performer's change through someone he used to drown out.$q$, $q$The bass player says "I am used to not being noticed," which places the story with those Caspian overpowered. Caspian never explains himself ("I do not think he ever said he had been too loud"), so he is not the narrator.$q$, 'draft', 'ef91595a-cd70-58eb-906b-5331fee2fab5')
