   $q$Text 1 presents the loss of the echo as a mysterious event. How does Text 2 transform this element?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It turns the loss into a punishment, since the director removes Caspian from the next concert.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It keeps the loss mysterious, since no one in the band can explain why the monitor stopped working.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It makes the loss a deliberate choice by a teacher, turning a magical consequence into a practical teaching method.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It drops the loss entirely, since Caspian changes only after the audience complains about him.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It makes the loss a deliberate choice by a teacher, turning a magical consequence into a practical teaching method.$q$, $q$In the legend the echo simply "had left," but Ms. Albescu turns the monitor on purpose and explains why: "listen to us." Caspian plays at the next concert, so the director does not punish him.$q$, 'draft', 'ef91595a-cd70-58eb-906b-5331fee2fab5')
