values
  ('8e83a7dd-f713-5fe3-b6a2-df7442214854', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-context-clues'), null, 'hard',
   $q$In paragraph 2, Coach Adebayo tells the crew to "Feather cleanly." In this context, "feather" is a verb that means to:$q$, $q$[{"text":"turn the oar blade flat so it passes above the water","is_correct":true},{"text":"row very gently so that the stroke takes no effort","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"surface-association"},{"text":"cover something with a soft layer of bird plumage","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"other-meaning-of-word"},{"text":"steer the whole boat in a smooth and gradual curve","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$turn the oar blade flat so it passes above the water$q$, $q$Lucia explains that "a rower turns the oar blade flat so it skims above the water instead of catching the wind," which is what feathering means here. The idea of something light like a feather is tempting, but the text describes the blade's position, not how hard the rower pulls.$q$, 'draft', '06099065-6c2d-5197-af3d-41dd0bd19709')
