   $q$Which statement most accurately reflects how strong the study's conclusions are, according to the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They are worthless, since weather alone explains the difference in moth counts.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstatement"},{"text":"They are certain, since the results were the same for two full summers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-limitations"},{"text":"They are promising but limited, since only two roads were compared and weather varies.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They are strong only for orange lamps, since that was the type the study tested most.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They are promising but limited, since only two roads were compared and weather varies.$q$, $q$Mensah-Larsen "cautions that two roads are a small sample and that weather can change moth numbers," yet the council still acted on the clear differences. The passage says weather can affect numbers, not that it explains the whole difference, so "worthless" goes too far.$q$, 'draft', 'be6f3449-9508-5af4-ba78-21ded9c58cc3')
