  ('6f260825-b159-5f4b-bfb7-3e424d773536', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-evidence-inference'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which detail provides the strongest evidence that sunlight caused most of the fading?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The guild's symbol was a golden shuttle crossed by two threads.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"The banner had greeted visitors in the entrance hall for nearly a century.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-vague"},{"text":"A strip hidden behind a wooden rail kept nearly its original color while the window side faded most.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Under a microscope, the silk fibers turned out to be brittle throughout.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-vague"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A strip hidden behind a wooden rail kept nearly its original color while the window side faded most.$q$, $q$The comparison between the shaded strip and the window side isolates light as the difference, so it is the strongest evidence. Brittle fibers show damage but do not by themselves point to sunlight as the cause.$q$, 'draft', '3f359569-85c4-592a-a1f7-a3538eb0a627')
