   $q$According to the passage, what can the signal priority system do when a bus approaches a light that is about to turn red?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It stops pedestrians from pressing the crossing button.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It sends a warning to cars on the side streets to slow down.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It holds the green light for a few extra seconds.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It turns the light green instantly so the bus never has to stop.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It holds the green light for a few extra seconds.$q$, $q$The second paragraph says "the signal can hold the green for a few extra seconds." It also states that the system "never changes a light instantly," so the first choice contradicts the text.$q$, 'draft', '2a608e7a-88c7-5ab8-b406-52d9b9a1ba2e')
